module test.claim.fleet.srv1_root_mutation_workflow_witness

// THE EMITTED srv1 ROOT-MUTATION JOBS, as gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow projects them: the gate step
// before any root step, the mode bound at job level, the approved selection covering every input a root step
// consumes, and the fleet key held only after the approval that authorizes it.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS APART FROM test.claim.fleet.srv1_root_mutation_approval_witness (split 2026-11-05,
// gunbc#15901). Those six claims read the emitted Job/Step structures, so they need the projecting module in
// their closure; that module is 7.8k lines and its typecheck alone outran the witness harness's 90-minute
// budget, which meant the seventeen gate-fold claims sharing the file never reached a verdict either. A
// witness that cannot run proves nothing, so the expensive closure is now paid only where it is spent: this
// file imports the projection, the approval witness no longer does. No claim here is a copy of one from that
// file, and the helpers below serve only these claims.
//
// DESIGN 3 still decides what each claim touches: it asserts over the EMITTED shape, the workflow's own
// output, and never re-derives a gate decision -- the decisions themselves are witnessed at the fold, in the
// other file, one interface apiece.

